DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccttffmmeerrggee utility merges several CTF (Compact C Type Format) data sec‐
     tions from several files into one output file, unifying common data.

     The following options are available:

     --ff      Match global symbols to global CTF data.

     --gg      Don't delete the original debugging sections.

     --ss      Use the .dynsym ELF section instead of the .symtab ELF section.

     --tt      Make sure that all object files have a CTF section.

     --vv      Enable verbose mode.

     --ll _l_a_b_e_l
             Sets the label as _l_a_b_e_l.

     --LL _l_a_b_e_l_e_n_v
             Instructs ccttffmmeerrggee to read the label from the environment vari‐
             able _l_a_b_e_l_e_n_v.

     --oo _o_u_t_f_i_l_e
             Use _o_u_t_f_i_l_e to store the merged CTF data.

     --dd _u_n_i_q_f_i_l_e
             Uniquify against _u_n_i_q_f_i_l_e.

     --dd _u_n_i_q_l_a_b_e_l
             Uniquify against label _u_n_i_q_l_a_b_e_l

     --ww _w_i_t_h_f_i_l_e
             Additive merge with _w_i_t_h_f_i_l_e.

     --cc _s_r_c_f_i_l_e _d_e_s_t_f_i_l_e
             Copy CTF data from _s_r_c_f_i_l_e into _d_e_s_t_f_i_l_e.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The ccttffmmeerrggee utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

